PATCH 509: twelve more cockpit-HUD paint/input methods (848c, 849f, 84c5, 84d8, 8503, 8516, 853f, 8558,
8573, 8590, 85bd, 85da).

Same family as patches 503/504/506/508.  BX is the display-list element's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET (the 209e
walk publishes it to DGROUP:0x3e08, patch 142) and DAT_2000_2d34 the PLAYER's near offset (patch 300);
Ghidra dereferenced both as host pointers, emitted the WORD inc/dec pairs as 4-byte read-modify-writes,
dropped the `lcall [0x6b4]` argument pairs, and for the input handlers dropped the clc/stc contract the
walk consumes.

GLYPH PLATES -- `mov di,[0x6d34]; movzbw ax,[di+0x3f]; add ax,K; lea bx,[bx+4]; [incw (bx); incw
[bx+2];] lcall [0x6b4] [; decw (bx); decw [bx+2]]`:
    848c  K=0x488   84c5  K=0x728   8503  K=0x4b8   853f  K=0x498   8558  K=0x4a8
    8573  K=0x4e8 (with the inc/dec pair)          85bd  K=0x4f8 (with the inc/dec pair)

INPUT HANDLERS -- `test ax,0x80; je -> stc` / `test ax,1; jne -> clc`, then
`xorb [di+0x3f],8; movb [di+F],3`, and on bits 0x14 a tail:
    849f  F=0xed, tail `call 0xa345` with DI live
    84d8  F=0xee, tail `movb [di+0x3f],0; lcall 0f69:8bb0` (== linear 0x18240, FUN_1000_8240)
    8516  F=0xef, plus `call 0xaae8` BEFORE the 0x14 test, tail `call 0xa751`, both with DI live
    8590  F=0xf7, tail `cmpb [di+0x8d],8; jae ..; shlb [di+0x8d],1`   (zoom in)
    85da  F=0xf6, tail `cmpb [di+0x8d],1; je ..;  shrb [di+0x8d],1`   (zoom out)

85bd was the top SIGSEGV of the post-508 sweep (85bd <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a).
